<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Bolsonaro clash in bitter debate ahead of election runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85295456ec4c5d5056baf86e2dfabe55f14132b9a53c187b99d3c5855704e037</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T03:42:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-lula-bolsonaro-debate-election-runoff--dc34142a5ff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-lula-bolsonaro-debate-election-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and right-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro traded personal attacks in a heated presidential debate on Sunday, a week before a closely contested runoff. The rivals accused each other of lying and corruption while clashing over the economy, security and healthcare ahead of the October 25 vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Louvre's $100 million crown jewels still missing one year after daring heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e75ce22a540362cbf3bc0b398adbcfb99ab661730bd881688f02ea67be0d8e60</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T02:01:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-louvre-100-million-crown-jewels-one-year-heist--ec7d1e08194d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-louvre-100-million-crown-jewels-one-year-heist" /><summary type="html">A year after thieves stole $100 million worth of crown jewels from Paris’s Louvre Museum, four suspects remain jailed awaiting trial, but the treasures are still missing. The October 19 heist saw thieves disguised as workers steal eight historic items, including jewellery belonging to Empress Eugenie, Napoleon III’s wife.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian military base fire kills at least four, injures dozens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d22e7a70f2de9f667ccfba106ac170c1c0f34c6832f2a2907e592f0a3b48a7f</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T22:16:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised--e89b96884cf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised" /><summary type="html">Four Canadian service members were killed and 39 people hospitalised after a fire broke out during military training at a base in Alberta on Saturday, officials said. Premier Danielle Smith said Sunday that at least 19 patients were in critical condition, with some suffering severe burns requiring prolonged intensive treatment.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky holds US talks as Trump accuses him of not wanting peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd98ad8fabf07c587c5d22b113417da7aa5b429abe938b1ad4a958313fab269e</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T21:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions--71a514130b55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky spoke with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner on Sunday amid tensions after President Donald Trump accused Kyiv of resisting peace with Russia. The talks came as both sides exchanged attacks on energy infrastructure, while Washington’s easing of Russian sanctions raised concerns among European allies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Macron says 'nothing justifies' violence in protests during address to nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:768b462a22706dcb2cf05f021fe5858a398b70f784c704994aa5c8db6dbe13c2</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T19:03:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation--374250dd9ba9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says 'nothing justifies' violence in protests during address to nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd9f940c8be48da94fd8c2c52918a77f1467191ae48516320aee0e960eb00959</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T18:44:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation--374250dd9ba9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said that "nothing justifies" violence during an address to the nation on Sunday, a day after demonstrations drew hundreds of thousands of people to the streets to protest the rising cost of living and poor school conditions. Police arrested more than 2,300 people over the weekend after violent groups clashed with officers and looted shops.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French President Emmanuel Macron addresses the nation after unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d419b56dce3f1dcb7eb3125f9727e03bde09e13501ca4ce703ae56cf9a5e1df9</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T18:33:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-replay-french-president-emmanuel-macron-addresses-the-nation-after-unrest--8684d32f906d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-replay-french-president-emmanuel-macron-addresses-the-nation-after-unrest" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Sunday vowed there would be "full transparency" over the response by security forces to protests that turned violent this weekend, after criticism that police preparations had been inadequate.</summary></entry><entry><title>French Riots: A Gift for Le Pen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d191aba3c9b45400b88cd1ffb5328876b171b37ff89eb93844b096e4fcaf9d2</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T18:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261018-french-riots-a-gift-for-le-pen--f3d0fac2590a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261018-french-riots-a-gift-for-le-pen" /><summary type="html">How much damage has the unrest in France caused to a protest movement rooted in genuine grievances but hijacked by rioters, violence and vandalism? Is it a gift to Marine Le Pen, the far-right leader and presidential frontrunner? Or is it a spectre of trouble to come in a deeply polarised society, amid an increasingly poisonous political atmosphere?
 
France 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to French analyst Renaud Foucault and a senior professor of economics.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Watch live: Macron to address France day after nationwide violent protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b3999065fed517b7e02b5c030d094c1d0954d22998b9d9064336f6a7f9ab54</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T17:55:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'France is burning', country 'shattered' by immigration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b414bc3a0a480aecf993bcea0f9ebfb99970102fdfe9389fa56a573038b0d1</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:54:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-trump-says-france-is-burning-country-shattered-by-immigration--2f747d7aa2b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-trump-says-france-is-burning-country-shattered-by-immigration" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday blamed immigration for unrest during protests in France and urged the country to tighten its migration rules. Washington bureau chief David Smith tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Renewed clashes in Paris: "We've seen numerous CRS charges to disperse protesters"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d09e7e78cf71a8010f0e901cf5711084399db6686d360314c4bebca8cee2d03</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:53:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-renewed-clashes-in-paris-we-ve-seen-numerous-crs-charges-to-disperse-protesters--fa1a15e1cdbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-renewed-clashes-in-paris-we-ve-seen-numerous-crs-charges-to-disperse-protesters" /><summary type="html">Fresh clashes broke out in Paris on Sunday, a day after France experienced one of its worst bouts of unrest in years. Protests over high prices left one demonstrator dead, thousands arrested, and shops across the country looted or damaged. France 24's Antonia Kerrigan tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli settlers attack European diplomats, beat French mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16c29431e2654f016b75167edb53c5c111983d6938ea46f50507ae5c202b9315</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:51:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-israeli-settlers-attack-european-diplomats-beat-french-mayor--d709ca30e6c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-israeli-settlers-attack-european-diplomats-beat-french-mayor" /><summary type="html">Israeli settlers attacked a convoy of European diplomats in the West Bank and beat up a visiting French mayor on Saturday, witnesses said, while US Secretary of State Marco Rubio warned against a brewing "crisis" in the territory a day after an American photojournalist was injured in a brutal attack.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests: "There's a constant back and forth over who's actually responsible"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f59242130f9a7cdd3ee0c1f45389f484f75f9cee66ddd7db3db0d197998dd45</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:49:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-there-s-a-constant-back-and-forth-over-who-s-actually-responsible--7be642619086.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-there-s-a-constant-back-and-forth-over-who-s-actually-responsible" /><summary type="html">The government has blamed the violence on hard-left and ultra-left groups, as well as criminals it says instigated the looting. We discuss this with international affairs commentator Matthew-Mary Caruchet and our reporter Antonia Kerrigan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump endorses embattled Israeli PM Netanyahu ahead of October 27 election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae8fdc7db704a04b28f952b7ea3e602501f1410cb7844268fce68a1c2cd5d0e6</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261018-trump-endorses-embattled-israeli-pm-netanyahu-ahead-of-october-27-election--a8f46cc8a76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261018-trump-endorses-embattled-israeli-pm-netanyahu-ahead-of-october-27-election" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday endorsed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ahead of Israel's October 27 elections. It was not clear what impact the endorsement would have on voters, since many Israelis have expressed disappointment with Trump over the outcome of the Iran war and the US president's ceasefire proposal.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Paris police clash with demonstrators and looters as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a2786a575253e59d2cbd0ae384fb9b2ca50eeeacf691145d55689f2449ef9f0</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:11:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-paris-police-in-new-battles-with-protesters-and-looters--c703dc13b30c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-paris-police-in-new-battles-with-protesters-and-looters" /><summary type="html">Paris police clashed with protesters and looters on Sunday as France reeled from nationwide demonstrations over the cost of living a day earlier that saw nearly 2,400 people arrested. Local authorities said that some 550,000 people took part in protests across France on Saturday, while organisers counted about 800,000</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: France’s CRS riot police deployed again in Paris as unrest continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32162044eaf7e60591c396fcf47b4ffde33a647f8b300d60c72287f582acbbcc</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T15:40:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /></entry><entry><title>Who capped Starlink in Ukraine? Musk, Trump and Rubio give three different answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad56007aeadbec9deee0d403009667ed2466985a5188f6f62e167eac1d3fd3a5</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T14:51:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261018-who-capped-starlink-in-ukraine-musk-trump-and-rubio-give-three-different-answers--1e7433bc79a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261018-who-capped-starlink-in-ukraine-musk-trump-and-rubio-give-three-different-answers" /><summary type="html">Ukraine says speed limits on Starlink are still hampering military efforts to fight off Russian drones, days after a surprise network slowdown that Kyiv called deliberate and Washington denied ordering.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>'Like we had a war': France left reeling after nationwide violent protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:763af5d9a672243c13155959b291ecbe916ca53edaa5b9cfd31b7fe626e168db</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-like-we-had-a-war-france-left-reeling-after-nationwide-violent-protests--b4098633db7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-like-we-had-a-war-france-left-reeling-after-nationwide-violent-protests" /><summary type="html">France on Sunday is dealing with the aftermath of nationwide protests that damaged around 1,500 businesses and caused losses estimated at hundreds of millions of euros. Police arrested an estimated 1,800 people across the country during Saturday's demonstrations over the cost of living and school conditions.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Escalating protests across Europe and the tragic capsize of a migrant boat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c2be687e75d545449199f509a225189953a2813580037c44c41773216e732e7</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:36:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-the-week-in-pictures-escalating-protests-across-europe-and-the-tragic-capsize-of-a-migrant---5793e5849bbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-the-week-in-pictures-escalating-protests-across-europe-and-the-tragic-capsize-of-a-migrant-boat" /><summary type="html">From student protests and heightened tensions across French demonstrations on October 17, to ongoing anti-government marches in Albania and the tragic sinking of a migrant boat off the coast of Djibouti, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Like we had a war': France counts cost of violent protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6cbd540669597a574e6a7ed546c6b9cdb63b5894734d5cdc462b82c7389d616</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-like-we-had-a-war-france-counts-cost-of-violent-protests--5386b0498b94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-like-we-had-a-war-france-counts-cost-of-violent-protests" /><summary type="html">France was reeling on Sunday from widespread damage caused by violent protests the day before that saw 1,800 people arrested, a historic town hall torched and widespread looting.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests: "There's a whole range of grievances at play"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2643a76cc7b8f86aeae9eb82aafa690bb40e28a98e2895709519c97e4779c2bc</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-there-s-a-whole-range-of-grievances-at-play--ad2db08ec5dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-there-s-a-whole-range-of-grievances-at-play" /><summary type="html">Is the anger in France driven more by declining living standards or by the perception that the economic burden is being distributed unfairly? We discuss this with our guest, Joseph Downing, senior lecturer in politics and international relations at Aston University.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Trump says 'France is burning', blames 'immigration' for nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a4907c094aff759d74ce2bf8d250f728262ce9aacafc27e49f4922f2a835136</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T12:57:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drone attack on Saint Petersburg kills one, sets refinery ablaze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5dbbcac23a2600dec72cd79806871bd26bc144ea38bf5116c5596fd616126fd</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T12:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack--5c56492efee9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">A large-scale Ukrainian drone attack on Russia's second-largest city Saint Petersburg killed at least one person and hospitalised another five on Sunday. The attack – which also sparked fires at an oil refinery and depot – comes as Kyiv accused Russia of violating Washington's "energy ceasefire" dozens of times.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris protests: A look at the aftermath</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d0bd94ab398f45f6e3a8d963cac23291fe9f1967dc0e4d4301413fd8d74feec</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:51:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-paris-protests-a-look-at-the-aftermath--b7e03a0edb66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-paris-protests-a-look-at-the-aftermath" /><summary type="html">Following yesterday's demonstrations in Paris, where violent clashes erupted between police and protesters, our reporter Antonia Kerrigan returns to place de la République.</summary></entry></feed>
